                <pb facs="0577" n="512" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg512"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">767.68119/898: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Istanbul</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-04-21T15:00:00+02:00">April 21, 1936—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 21—11:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>12. Department’s 17, April 20, 5 p.m. Reports are officially denied. While such a
                    move might be welcomed by military its execution at the present time seems
                    highly unlikely in view of the nature of Turkish diplomatic <hi
                        rendition="#italic">démarche</hi> concerning Straits and reception generally
                    accorded to it.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
